    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9e06b592-203c-53cd-99bc-4f89e4cebf23",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N.; The Apple Dumpling Gang; Truck Stop Women; Mackintosh and T.J.; Stay Hungry; King Kong; The Shadow of Chikara; Goin' South; The Wild Women of Chastity Gulch; Maverick; Bootleggers; Creature from Black Lake\n- People: Walt Disney; Dick Van Dyke; Bill Bixby; Dennis Fimple\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: U.S. Navy pilot; Russell Donovan\n- Topics: comedy films; comedy-western films; castaways; California Gold Rush\n\nFacts:\n- Walt Disney released and scripted the 1966 comedy film Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N..\n- Dick Van Dyke starred in Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N. as a U.S. Navy pilot who becomes a castaway on a tropical island.\n- Dennis Fimple shared the lead in the 1974 film Bootleggers.\n- Dennis Fimple appeared in the 1974 film Truck Stop Women.\n- Walt Disney Productions produced the 1975 American comedy-western film The Apple Dumpling Gang.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang is about slick gambler Russell Donovan, played by Bill Bixby, who is duped into caring for orphans who later strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- Dennis Fimple appeared in The Apple Dumpling Gang and Mackintosh and T.J. in 1975.\n- Dennis Fimple shared the lead in the 1976 film Creature from Black Lake.\n- Dennis Fimple appeared in Stay Hungry and King Kong in 1976, The Shadow of Chikara in 1977, Goin' South in 1978, The Wild Women of Chastity Gulch in 1982, and Maverick in 1994.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6eb21996-ab4c-5fac-a790-c629d446aced",
        "text": "Page: Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N.. Sentence: Lt. Robin Crusoe USN is a 1966 comedy film released and scripted by Walt Disney, and starring Dick Van Dyke as a U.S. Navy pilot who becomes a castaway on a tropical island.\nPage: The Apple Dumpling Gang (film). Sentence: The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped into taking care of a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\nPage: Dennis Fimple. Sentence: He also had roles in films such as \"Truck Stop Women\" (1974), \"The Apple Dumpling Gang\" (1975), \"Mackintosh and T.J.\" (1975), \"Stay Hungry\" (1976), \"King Kong\" (1976), \"The Shadow of Chikara\" (1977), \"Goin' South\" (1978), \"The Wild Women of Chastity Gulch\" (1982) and \"Maverick\" (1994), and shared the lead in \"Bootleggers\" (1974) and \"Creature from Black Lake\" (1976).",
